TEXT 480 184 Left 4 ;LOADS
TEXT -520 16 Left 2 ;At startup plant1 has 20MW, plant2 has 100MW, plant3 has 20MW\nThe initial load at startup is 140MW \nAfter 1s the additional load with 20MW is switched on\nThe primary regulation of plant1 starts and after 3s delivers the additional 20MW \nof the switched load. The frequency sinks from 50Hz to 49.915Hz\nThe difference to the nominal frequency at 50Hz remains because of the proportional control of plant1\nAt 4s the secondary regulation of plant2 starts and after additional 4s the frequency is again at 50Hz (integral controller)\nThe power output of plant1 decrease until the initial value of 20MW is reached again\nThe power output of plant2 increase about 20MW to the final value of 120MW\nAt 10s plant3 start to output more power and after 5s the ouput of power is increased from 20MW to 40MW\nAt the same time the ouput power of plant2 is reduced about 20MW to 100MW again. \nAt the end the whole power output is 160MW the load is 160MW and the frequency is 50Hz\nThe power level of the regulated (Primary and secondary) plant1 and 2 is like at the start of the \nsimulation and is ready for a new change in the power value (of a load or of a plant)
TEXT -24 416 Left 2 ;NOTE:\nThe delay of the secondary regulation is\ndone by setting the enable input of the\nPI-controller to 4s
TEXT -320 168 Left 4 ;NOTE: For simplicity all three synchronous generators in this example has the same nominal values
